WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.132
LAG is used when a question contains words such as previous, change, or time since.

00:00:05.132 --> 00:00:07.917
The current row remains in the result.

00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:12.227
LAG retrieves a value from an earlier row in the defined order.

00:00:12.227 --> 00:00:17.612
Partitioning prevents one patient's sequence from mixing with another patient's sequence.

00:00:17.612 --> 00:00:21.057
The order is part of the definition of previous.

00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:26.687
LAG and LEAD compare a row with a previous or next row in a defined sequence.

00:00:26.687 --> 00:00:31.892
The sequence must be meaningful—usually time plus a stable tie-breaker.

00:00:31.892 --> 00:00:37.822
This is powerful for readmissions, repeat purchases, machine events, and state transitions.
